# Product Intelligence Spec
**AI PM Learner — adaptive digest + quiz platform**

---

## Why this doc exists

The deployment, hosting, and CI/CD are table stakes — any engineer can figure those out.
The USP of this product lives in three places:

1. How well-curated the daily digest is (the hook that brings you back)
2. How well agents hand off context to each other (the intelligence layer)
3. How gracefully the system handles failure (the trust layer)

---

## System overview

```
[Celery 7am trigger]
        ↓
[Content Curation Agent]  ←— reads: syllabus_state, read_history (Supabase)
        |                  ←— tools: web_search, fetch_article, dedup_check (pgvector)
        | ContentToAssessmentContext (Pydantic, validated)
        ↓
[Assessment Agent]         ←— reads: top_chunks (pgvector RAG), question_history
        |                  ←— tools: retrieve_chunks, generate_question, evaluate_answer
        | QuizResult (Pydantic, validated)
        ↓
[Adaptive Engine]          ←— runs: SM-2 algorithm
        |                  ←— writes: new syllabus_state, next_review_date
        ↓
[Supabase]                 ←— user reads digest + takes quiz via Next.js frontend
```

Orchestration layer: LangGraph state machine
Each node is a Python function. Each edge is a conditional based on agent output.
Max steps: 12 (hard cap — prevents infinite loops, the n8n failure mode).

