## 1. Content Curation Agent

### The goal
Return the 2 best articles for this specific user on this specific day.
Not 2 random articles on "RAG". The 2 that fill their exact current gap.

### What "best" means — the quality rubric

Every candidate article is scored across 5 dimensions:

| Dimension | How it's measured | Weight |
|---|---|---|
| Source reputation | Whitelist: Anthropic=10, HF=9, arXiv=8, TDS=6, Medium=3, unknown=skip | 25% |
| Recency | <30d=10, <90d=7, <1yr=4, older=skip | 20% |
| Level match | LLM scores: does the article's depth match the user's current level (1–5)? | 25% |
| Novelty | Cosine similarity vs read history in pgvector. >0.85 = skip | 20% |
| Concept density | LLM scores: how many distinct learnable concepts does this article contain? | 10% |

**Open question:** Are these weights right? Validate after 2 weeks of real usage by
checking whether users score higher on topics where level_match was >0.8.

### How the search intent is built

The agent reads the user's `syllabus_state` and constructs a search query
that encodes level + weak concept + recency requirement:

```
Level 2, weak on "RAG retrieval strategies":
→ "RAG retrieval strategies practical tutorial 2025"

Level 4, weak on "agentic AI evaluation":
→ "agentic AI evaluation metrics production 2025 advanced"

NOT just: "RAG" or "agentic AI"
```

The query template is part of the agent's system prompt. It must be updated
when new topics are added to the syllabus.

### Diversity rule

The 2 articles must come from different domains.
If both top candidates share a domain, take #1 and #3.

Always include one "AI PM pulse" article — what's happening in the field this week —
alongside the deep-dive on the user's current weak topic. This mirrors how real
PMs stay current: one depth item, one breadth item per day.

### Curation rationale — the handoff note

After selecting articles, the agent writes a plain-English note explaining why:

> "User scored 0.31 on retrieval strategies 8 days ago. Article 1 is a practical
> chunking guide from HuggingFace. Article 2 covers hybrid search as a contrast.
> Recommend quiz focuses on the fixed-size vs semantic chunking tradeoff."

This note travels to the Assessment Agent. It is the difference between
a targeted quiz and a generic one.

**Do not skip this step to save tokens.** The quality degradation is visible immediately.

### Chunking and embedding

- Chunk size: 500 tokens, 50-token overlap
- Embedding model: `text-embedding-3-small` (OpenAI) or equivalent
- Store in: Supabase pgvector extension (free, no separate vector DB needed at MVP scale)
- Dedup check: run cosine similarity against last 14 days of the user's read history

