## 6. Open Questions (resolve during build)

These are decisions we haven't made yet. Answer them with real data after 2 weeks of usage.

| Question | Why it matters | How to decide |
|---|---|---|
| Are the quality rubric weights right? | Directly affects content relevance | Track: do higher level_match scores → higher quiz scores? |
| What's the right chunk size? | Affects retrieval precision | A/B test 300 vs 500 vs 800 tokens on quiz score outcomes |
| How many topics per onboarding? | Too many = shallow coverage, too few = boredom | Start with 3 forced, cap at 6 |
| When to introduce a new topic vs reinforce existing? | Pacing affects retention | After user hits level 3 on current topics, introduce one new one |
| Should the AI PM pulse article always be included? | Breadth vs depth tradeoff | Track engagement: do users open the pulse article? After 30 days, cut or keep |
| What does "level 5" actually look like for each topic? | Without definition, the rubric is vague | Write level descriptors for each topic before building the rubric prompt |

